cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "This is in-progress research. Please treat any citation as referring to a draft, not a peer-reviewed source."
title: "Exploring the Use of Artificial Intelligence and Music-Based Therapy in Supporting Individuals with Drug Addiction and Substance Use Disorder"
authors:
  - family-names: "Godwin Bernard"
    given-names: "Bernard"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add if you have one
abstract: >-
  A scoping review culminating in a proposed conceptual framework, reported
  against PRISMA-ScR, examining how artificial intelligence tools and
  music-based therapeutic interventions can function as adjuncts to
  professional treatment for people with a substance use disorder (SUD). The
  review scope is SUD-wide, not AUD-anchored; alcohol use disorder receives
  particular attention as the sub-population where the AI literature is
  densest, and broader SUD evidence is admitted and flagged where
  substance-specific work is absent. The work is organised around four
  pillars: emotional regulation, craving reduction, self-expression, and
  personalised recovery support.
keywords:
  - substance use disorder
  - alcohol use disorder
  - music therapy
  - artificial intelligence
  - affective computing
  - recovery support
  - scoping review
date-released: 2026-06-19
